<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

<h2>Purpose</h2>
<p><code>Timer</code> is a tiny development middleware that logs duration, method, and path after the handler returns, as a <code>log/slog</code> record "request timed" at Info to <code>slog.Default()</code>.</p>
<pre><code>r.Use(middleware.Timer)</code></pre>

<h2>Output shape</h2>
<p>With the default <code>slog</code> handler:</p>
<pre><code>2026/10/22 09:41:00 INFO request timed duration=2.1ms method=GET path=/users</code></pre>

<h2>Options</h2>
<pre><code>r.Use(middleware.TimerWithOptions(middleware.TimerOptions{
    Logger: logger,
    Level:  slog.LevelDebug,
}))</code></pre>

<h2>Logger vs timer</h2>
<p>Use <code>Logger</code> for application request logs. Use <code>Timer</code> when you want a quick local timing view with minimal setup.</p>
</article>

